["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/FunctionalSafety/EvidenceType", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "EvidenceType refers to categories of documented or observable proof used to verify compliance, qualification, or performance", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/inspection", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "A thorough examination or checking of documentation, records, processes, or systems to confirm compliance or adherence. An inspection needs to have a defined set of acceptance criteria (e.g. a checklist), a documentation of roles involved in the inspection (e.g. to document the inspector's independence) and a clear documentation of when and how it was performed.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
